{"duration_api_ms":24158,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"87b423cc-f61e-4b07-8cb2-07f4c10785e8","total_cost_usd":0.12611340000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11985,"cache_read_input_tokens":150302,"output_tokens":1804,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":529},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11985},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":1804,"cacheReadInputTokens":150302,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11985,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.12611340000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":529,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":6,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I changed `Hijack` so it only refuses once body bytes have been written. Before, it also refused after just the headers were sent, for example after `WriteHeaderNow()`, which middleware and websocket upgrade code often call before hijacking. `go test ./...` passes.\n\n- **`response_writer.go:110`**: the check is now `w.size > 0` instead of `w.Written()`, with a one-line comment explaining why. The error message is now `\"gin: response body already written\"`.\n- **`response_writer_test.go`**: I added a test case where hijacking after `WriteHeaderNow()` succeeds.\n\nI couldn't commit: git has no user name or email set here. The changes are in the working tree, so you can commit them with your own identity.\n\nRisk: if a handler sets headers, sends them, and then hijacks, it now gets the raw connection instead of an error, with those headers already sent.","ttft_ms":4507,"type":"result","duration_ms":28871,"uuid":"e8973fac-7b6b-40a5-8c66-1554939f613d","ttft_stream_ms":1762,"time_to_request_ms":93,"first_content_frame_ms":1762,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
